                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Understanding 理解",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nPeyer's patches are lymphoid nodules located in the small intestine, where T cells congregate. Peyer's patches are most important in the secondary immune response, although they play a role in the primary immune response as well. These organs may enlarge as they become highly active in the immune response. The organs noted in the remaining options are incorrect.\n",
